text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)\\nSapseep Forest enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{G}, {T}: You gain 1 life. Activate only if you control two or more green permanents.', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', "At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, if that player has two or fewer cards in hand, Hellfire Mongrel deals 2 damage to that player.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may gain 1 life.', 'Blue spells and red spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Nightscape Familiar.', "Choose one —\\n• Naya Charm deals 3 damage to target creature.\\n• Return target card from a graveyard to its owner's hand.\\n• Tap all creatures target player controls.", "Choose one —\\n• Return target permanent to its owner's hand.\\n• Target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.\\n• Creatures you control get +2/+0 until end of turn.", "Choose two —\\n• Target player loses X life.\\n• Return target creature card with mana value X or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n• Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn.\\n• Up to X target creatures gain fear until end of turn. (They can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Counter target noncreature spell.', 'Counter target noncreature spell. Its controller loses 2 life.', 'Counter target spell. Its controller loses 3 life.', 'Crumbling Necropolis enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}, {B}, or {R}.', 'Double strike', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may gain 1 life.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has flying.\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, create a 2/2 white Griffin creature token with flying.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+3 and has flying.\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage to a player, that player discards two cards.', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2 and has trample and lifelink.\\nEquip {3}', 'Exalted (Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, that creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\n{1}, Sacrifice Qasali Pridemage: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nIslandcycling {2}, swampcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for an Island or Swamp card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)", "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nWhen Shriekmaw enters the battlefield, destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature.\\nEvoke {1}{B} (You may cast this spell for its evoke cost. If you do, it's sacrificed when it enters the battlefield.)", 'First strike\\nUnearth {U}{B}{R} ({U}{B}{R}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', "Flash\\nWhen Briarhorn enters the battlefield, target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.\\nEvoke {1}{G} (You may cast this spell for its evoke cost. If you do, it's sacrificed when it enters the battlefield.)", "Flash\\nWhen Fleetfoot Panther enters the battlefield, return a green or white creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flying, first strike\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Firemane Angel is in your graveyard or on the battlefield, you may gain 1 life.\\n{6}{R}{R}{W}{W}: Return Firemane Angel from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep.', 'Flying, haste\\nWhenever Blazing Specter deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 1 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Surveilling Sprite dies, you may draw a card.', 'Gain control of target creature. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Graypelt Refuge enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Graypelt Refuge enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', 'Haste\\nSwampcycling {2}, mountaincycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Swamp or Mountain card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', 'Jungle Shrine enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}, {G}, or {W}.', 'Kazandu Refuge enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Kazandu Refuge enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', "Kicker {1}{R} (You may pay an additional {1}{R} as you cast this spell.)\\nDestroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated. If this spell was kicked, Agonizing Demise deals damage equal to that creature's power to the creature's controller.", 'Kird Ape gets +1/+2 as long as you control a Forest.', 'Landfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may gain 2 life.', 'Lightning Helix deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.', 'Loam Lion gets +1/+2 as long as you control a Forest.', 'Look at the top five cards of your library. You may reveal any number of creature cards from among them and put the revealed cards into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", "Return target creature card from a graveyard and target creature on the battlefield to their owners' hands.", "Return target creature to its owner's hand. Its controller loses 1 life.", "Return target permanent to its owner's hand. Then that player discards a card.", 'Rupture Spire enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rupture Spire enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you pay {1}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Sacrifice Morgue Toad: Add {U}{R}.', 'Target opponent sacrifices a creature, discards three cards, then loses 5 life. You return a creature card from your graveyard to your hand, draw three cards, then gain 5 life.', 'Target player discards a card.', 'Target player draws two cards.\\nFlashback—{1}{U}, Pay 3 life. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Target player gains 8 life.\\nBasic landcycling {1}{G} ({1}{G}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', 'Until end of turn, creatures you control get +5/+5 and gain first strike, trample, and lifelink.', "Vigilance\\n{R}, {T}: Target creature can't block this turn.\\n{G}, {T}: Target creature blocks this turn if able.", 'When Brackwater Elemental attacks or blocks, sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.\\nUnearth {2}{U} ({2}{U}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'When Loxodon Hierarch enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.\\n{G}{W}, Sacrifice Loxodon Hierarch: Regenerate each creature you control.', "When Ogre Savant enters the battlefield, if {U} was spent to cast it, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Steamcore Weird enters the battlefield, if {R} was spent to cast it, it deals 2 damage to any target.', 'When Sylvan Ranger enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Whenever Dimir Cutpurse deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card and you draw a card.', 'Whenever Slavering Nulls deals combat damage to a player, if you control a Swamp, you may have that player discard a card.', 'Whenever Spitemare is dealt damage, it deals that much damage to any target.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.', "Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Ajani's Pridemate.", 'Whenever you gain life, put that many +1/+1 counters on Ageless Entity.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {2}. If you do, Searing Meditation deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Wild Nacatl gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Mountain.\\nWild Nacatl gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Plains.', "You may have Pride of Lions assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "[+1]: Target permanent doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\\n[−2]: Ajani Vengeant deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.\\n[−7]: Destroy all lands target player controls.", "[+3]: Destroy target noncreature permanent.\\n[−2]: Gain control of target creature.\\n[−9]: Nicol Bolas, Planeswalker deals 7 damage to target player or planeswalker. That player or that planeswalker's controller discards seven cards, then sacrifices seven permanents.", '{1}, {T}: Tap target artifact, creature, or land.', '{2}{G}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{G}{W}, {T}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', '{T}: Add {U}, {B}, or {R}.']
flavor: ['"Don\'t be fooled. If it were as docile as it looks, it would\'ve died off long ago."\\n—Yon Basrel, Oran-Rief survivalist', '"He hasn\'t returned to the Cloud Forest. But I can still sense his calming presence."\\n—Zaliki of Naya', '"I have lived long, and I remember how this city once was. If my death serves to bring back the Ravnica in my memory, then so be it."', '"I knew a creature carved from a dream of wild freedom. Any attempt to leash or exploit it failed, and at terrible cost."\\n—Ashling', '"Looks like we\'re completely outnumbered."\\n"Lucky for us. I thought we\'d be bored."', '"May this grant you all the strength of the behemoths and none of their serenity."\\n—Ajani', '"No fact escapes me. Why do you think you can?"', '"Not all paths are found on the forest floor."', '"Rage is not the answer. Rage followed by fitting vengeance is the answer."\\n—Ajani', '"Relative of yours?" Ertai teased. Mirri simply sneered.', '"Retribution is best delivered by claws and rage, with both magnified."\\n—Ajani', '"So many choices. Shall I choose loathing, hate, or malice today?"\\n—Eliza of the Keep', '"The Cloud Nacatl sit and think, a bunch of soft paws. We are the Claws of Marisi, stalking, pouncing, drawing blood."', '"The essence of every world, every spell, and every thought is power. Nothing else matters, because nothing else exists."\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"The more our numbers grow, the more I gain hope that Volrath and his cursed stronghold will one day fall."\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"The toads of Urborg aren\'t fast, powerful, or pleasant, but they have their uses."\\n—Ertai', '"They say the ruins of Sedraxis were once a shining capital in Vithia. Now it is a blight, a place to be avoided by the living."\\n—Olcot, Rider of Joffik', '"This creature is inadequate. Send it to the splicers for innovation."\\n—Malcator, Executor of Synthesis', '"Touched by moroii"\\n—Undercity slang meaning "to grow old"', '"We are one with the wild things. Life blooms from our fingertips and nature responds to our summons."\\n—Jade creed', '"We must hunt and kill the dragon before it can return to raze our ancient city."', '"When I meditate I see the world as it should be. All that does not fit, I remove."\\n—Alovnek, Boros guildmage', '"When one of us prospers, the pride prospers."\\n—Jazal Goldmane', '"Which would you like first, the insult or the injury?"', 'An elder in one pride, of the Sigiled caste in another.', 'Anything sent into a plagued world is bound to come back infected.', 'Apes can be gentle, contemplative beasts—but context is everything.', "Deep in nature's core lies a potential unsullied by greed or civilization.", 'Every world is an organism, able to grow new lands. Some just do it faster than others.', 'Having lost their minds, they now want yours.', "He's an oxymoron.", "In Zendikar, today's grassland could be tomorrow's jungle, and hunting grounds change as quickly as the weather.", 'In fire there is the spark of chaos and destruction, the seed of life. In ice there is perfect tranquility, perfect order, and the silence of death.', 'In the autumn, she casts her seeds across the streets below, and come spring, her children rise in service to the Conclave.', 'Kithkin somnomancers enjoy the peaceful dreams wafting from their victims.', 'Like many Izzet creations, weirds are based on wild contradictions yet somehow manage to work.', 'Like most features of Grixis, the obelisks that remain from the time of Alara now exist only for dark exploitation.', "Nicol Bolas doesn't distinguish between servants and victims.", "Nightscape masters don't stop at raising the spirit of a fallen battlemage. They raise the flesh along with it.", 'On Naya, ambition and treachery are scarce, hunted nearly to extinction by the awe owed to terrestrial gods.', 'One of the most ferocious and deadly gargantuans, the thoctar never sees its worshippers, but it often awakens surrounded by gifts and sacrifices.', 'Other guilds demand tolls from those who travel their territories, but not House Dimir. It takes its share secretly, one coin purse at a time.', 'Some who scouted new lands chose to stay.', 'Take two steps north into the unsettled future, south into the unquiet past, east into the present day, or west into the great unknown.', 'Taste his power, hunger for his command.', "Tel-Jilad's sworn protectors are the trolls, yet more fearsome protectors were created by the Tangle itself.", 'Their natural curiosity, combined with a knack for trespassing, makes sprites excellent spies.', 'There is always a greater power.', 'There is no fondness between the hound and its master. There is only a common appreciation of the hunt.', "There's only one thing worse than a hungry lion—many hungry lions."]
